      "message": "Nit: would you mind turning this into a kernel-doc comment like the other helpers in the P3S headers (e.g. `vma_file_offset_at()` in `include/linux/p3s/vma.h`), so that it explains the partial 16KB pages? Something like:\n\n```\n/*\n * vma_shmem_swap_usage - Swapped bytes of the file range a 4KB VMA maps\n * @vma: 4KB VMA of a shmem file\n * @start: Start of the address range in @vma\n * @end: End of the address range in @vma\n *\n * A 4KB VMA can start or end partway through a 16KB file page, so count\n * only the bytes of each swapped entry that [@start, @end) maps, rather\n * than whole entries.\n */\n```\n\nThe `#else` and `#endif` could also carry `/* !CONFIG_ARM64_PER_PROCESS_PAGE_SIZE */` and `/* CONFIG_ARM64_PER_PROCESS_PAGE_SIZE */`, as in `include/linux/p3s/mm.h`.",
